.TH "GIT-BUG" "1" "Apr 2019" "Generated from git-bug's source code" ""

.SH NAME
git-bug-bug-review-comment - Add a line-anchored comment to an existing review


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit-bug bug review comment REVIEW_ID [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Attach a line-anchored comment to an existing review thread on a
pull-request. REVIEW_ID is the review's combined id (or a unique prefix).

.PP
For new threads, supply --path and --line (optionally --end-line). For
replies to an existing review comment, supply --reply-to ; --path,
--line and --commit will default to those of the comment being replied to.

.PP
--commit defaults to the PR's current head commit.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--path\fP=""
	File path the comment anchors to

.PP
\fB--line\fP=0
	Start line (1-based) in the file

.PP
\fB--end-line\fP=0
	End line (inclusive). Defaults to --line for a single-line anchor.

.PP
\fB--reply-to\fP=""
	Combined id of a review comment to reply to

.PP
\fB--commit\fP=""
	Commit hash the comment is anchored to (defaults to PR head)

.PP
\fB-m\fP, \fB--message\fP=""
	Comment body

.PP
\fB-F\fP, \fB--file\fP=""
	Take the body from the given file (- for stdin)

.PP
\fB--non-interactive\fP[=false]
	Do not ask for user input

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for comment


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgit-bug-bug-review(1)\fP
